Bound the size of an f-string joined during inference. Each part of an
f-string could already infer to a string up to the per-operation cap, but
``JoinedStr`` concatenated the parts with no limit, so a short source such as
``f"{'a' * 90000000}" f"{'b' * 90000000}"`` materialized a multi-hundred-megabyte
string. The join now yields ``Uninferable`` past the same cap used for
repetition, concatenation and format width.

Refs #3467
